  "prediction": "The Older Americans Act (OAA), first enacted in 1965, is the primary federal legislation providing social services and nutrition programs for older adults. The report outlines the history and key provisions of the OAA, focusing on Title III grants, which fund supportive services for older adults. Title III grants are allocated based on a formula that takes into account the population of older adults in each state and the cost of living. The report also discusses the reauthorization of the OAA in 2016, which made changes to the funding formula and other provisions. The report highlights the importance of the OAA in providing essential services to older adults and the need for continued funding and support. The report also includes appendices with legislative history, population data, and funding comparisons. Overall, the report emphasizes the importance of the OAA in addressing the needs of older adults and the need for ongoing funding and support to ensure the effectiveness of the program.",
  "scored_prediction": "The Older Americans Act (OAA), first enacted in 1965, is the primary federal legislation providing social services and nutrition programs for older adults. The report outlines the history and key provisions of the OAA, focusing on Title III grants, which fund supportive services for older adults. Title III grants are allocated based on a formula that takes into account the population of older adults in each state and the cost of living. The report also discusses the reauthorization of the OAA in 2016, which made changes to the funding formula and other provisions. The report highlights the importance of the OAA in providing essential services to older adults and the need for continued funding and support. The report also includes appendices with legislative history, population data, and funding comparisons. Overall, the report emphasizes the importance of the OAA in addressing the needs of older adults and the need for ongoing funding and support to ensure the effectiveness of the program.",
